course: dictionary
lesson: 16176
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it, which are its context. «Mia saw XI on the clock face, so she knew it was eleven o'clock.» The clock tells you XI is a number here.
explain: «The England XI ran onto the pitch.» The word pitch and the players running on tell you that XI is a team here. An XI is a team of eleven players. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Xi Jinping is the leader of China.» Here Xi is a name, not a number or a team. Capital letters, and the name Jinping after it, are clues that it is a person.
fact: Xi is a Roman numeral. XI means 11, because 10 is X and 1 is I.
fact: Xi is the 14th letter of the Greek alphabet. It is written Ξ or ξ.
fact: In Chinese, Xi is a family name. It sounds like «shee».
fact: Xi Jinping is the leader of China, so you will often see Xi in news stories.
fact: In sport, an XI is a team of eleven players, such as a cricket or football team.
exercise: «Mia saw XI on the clock face.» What number does XI stand for? | 111 | *11 | 9 | 1
exercise: The Greek letter xi is written with which symbols? | *Ξ ξ | Σ σ | Ω ω | XI
exercise: «Xi Jinping is the leader of China.» What is Xi here? | A Roman numeral | *A family name | A football team | A Greek letter
test: «The England XI ran onto the pitch.» What does XI mean here? | A team of eleven players | A team of ten players | A cricket bat | *A team of eleven players, not a number
test: In Chinese, Xi sounds like which word? | zee | *shee | ex | ksee
exam: «The school asked for an XI for the match.» Which meaning of xi is this? | *A team of eleven players | A Roman numeral for 14 | A Chinese family name | A Greek letter
